I was referring to motherboards only as I am only interested in upgrading 
my present Cyrix 5x86. I used the 64 Mb of Ram and the video card to 
illustrate the disparity in the costs of the two boards. Also, I referred 
to a distaste for Intel-Microshaft, this is my opinion and maybe not 
shared by the group. This is what I want: a fast machine to run Linux and 
to perform scientific computing( FORTRAN) and various network and Gnu 
software programs. I don't care about running any Windows crap. Been 
there done that! I want the most bang for the buck as well. I guess I 
want to be SOLD a product (ie. explain to me why I should buy one product 
versus the others) which seems to not be the way business works these days. 
I guess I am a bit frustrated by marketing people as I am an engineer who 
buys products using common sense. Help!

Sorry Ray, I got crazy.

