I should add a warning somewhere about this.  The bottom line is that
Milo environment variables are not supported on the UDB right now.  So,
why are the "env" commands there?  Well, technically, there is no
difference between a UDB and a Noname - the environment commands are for
the Noname when Milo has been blown into flash.   The solution may be to
use a part of the NVRAM for Milo that is not being used by WNT, if I could
work out just where that is...

